WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.190 align:middle line:84%
I keep track of several
different calendars

2
00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:05.310 align:middle line:84%
through their iCal feeds and
my iCalendar application.

3
00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:07.230 align:middle line:84%
I use Apple iCal,
but this will work

4
00:00:07.230 --> 00:00:09.990 align:middle line:84%
with any iCal reader like
Microsoft Outlook, or Google

5
00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:12.180 align:middle line:90%
Calendar, or anything like that.

6
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:14.280 align:middle line:84%
With my Basecamp
calendars, I can

7
00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.815 align:middle line:84%
use their iCal feeds to
add them to my program.

8
00:00:16.815 --> 00:00:19.610 align:middle line:84%
If I just want to add a
specific projects calendar,

9
00:00:19.610 --> 00:00:22.260 align:middle line:84%
I'll open that project and
click on the calendar tab.

10
00:00:22.260 --> 00:00:25.320 align:middle line:84%
When I scroll down,
I'll see a link here

11
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.280 align:middle line:84%
where I can click on and
subscribe to iCalendar.

12
00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.840 align:middle line:84%
But if I really
want an iCal feed

13
00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:32.759 align:middle line:84%
of all the projects
on my Basecamp,

14
00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:34.230 align:middle line:90%
there's a better option.

15
00:00:34.230 --> 00:00:36.480 align:middle line:84%
I'll go back to the
dashboard, and then

16
00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.060 align:middle line:90%
scroll down to the bottom here.

17
00:00:39.060 --> 00:00:42.430 align:middle line:84%
I'll notice all my global
feeds in this section.

18
00:00:42.430 --> 00:00:44.430 align:middle line:84%
I'll click on the
Global iCalendar link,

19
00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:48.060 align:middle line:84%
and I'll open my iCal
program to add to it.

20
00:00:48.060 --> 00:00:51.300 align:middle line:84%
From there, I can set
these options how I want,

21
00:00:51.300 --> 00:00:53.460 align:middle line:84%
then just click
here to subscribe.

22
00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:56.190 align:middle line:84%
The events pull into my app
alongside all the other ones

23
00:00:56.190 --> 00:00:57.510 align:middle line:90%
I already have in there.

24
00:00:57.510 --> 00:01:00.210 align:middle line:84%
It's an easy way to keep
all of these calendars.

25
00:01:00.210 --> 00:01:02.090 align:middle line:90%
In one place.
